AGC CORE ROPE MEMORY  (Block II fixed ROM)

TYPE: transformer ROM  (not storage cores)
  Data lives in wire path, not magnetization.
  Core = pulse generator + transformer.
  Flip selected core → pulse only on wires that pass THROUGH it.

WIRES (per core, Block II):
  SET / RESET     2 lines   (common, all cores in plane)
  INHIBIT         ~7-10 pairs  (address decode)
  SENSE           192 lines    (data: 12 strands × 16 bits)

ENCODING
  Sense wire THROUGH core  →  1
  Sense wire AROUND  core  →  0

ORGANIZATION
  Word          = 16 bits  (15 data + 1 parity)
  Words / core  = 12       (192 bits)
  Cores / module= 512
  Words / module= 6144
  Modules       = 6
  Total words   = 36864    (~72 KB)

ADDRESSING
  Inhibit currents cancel SET on every core except the one whose
  address bits match the inactive inhibit set.
  Only that core flips.

READ CYCLE
  1. Drive SET + selected inhibits  → one core flips
  2. Pulse appears on the 16 sense wires of the chosen strand
     that threaded that core
  3. Sense amps latch the word
  4. RESET restores the core

FUNDAMENTALS
  Non-volatile, radiation-hard, unchangeable after weave.
  Density: 192 bits/core vs 1 bit/core in erasable RAM.
  Hand-woven (“LOL memory”).
